  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through next Sunday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Dry and quiet weather across central and\nnorthern Nevada today with a buildup of clouds moving in. Warmer\ntemperatures with highs reaching a few degrees above normal in the\n50s and 60s. The conditions are expected to persist over the \nregion until late afternoon in Humboldt County as the next weather\nsystem will move over western Nevada. Precipitation chances \nexpected to remain over Humboldt County until Monday afternoon \nwhen the front pushes further inland and covers central and \nnorthern Nevada. Much of the precipitation and high elevated snow \nwill occur from Monday afternoon and overnight into Tuesday \nmorning. Snow levels will rise above 8000 feet Monday afternoon, \nthen drop to around 4000-5000 feet (around 6000-7000 feet for \nNortheastern Nye, White Pine County, and eastern Elko County). For\nnorthern Nevada, up to a trace to half an inch of snow is \nexpected along the I-80 corridor with higher elevated areas along \nNV-225, Emigrant Pass and Pequop summit seeing a 20-40% of an \ninch or more. For central Nevada, up to trace to one inch of snow \nin the valleys with higher elevated areas along the US-50 corridor\nseeing a 35-60% chance of up to an inch or more of snow, while \nthe high passes and summits have a 25-50% chance of seeing two \ninches of snow. Cooling temperature trend along with the storm \nfront has highs dropping to near normal in the 40s to 50s Monday, \nthen just a few degrees below normal on Tuesday in the 30s to low \n40s.\n\nThere will be a short break in the weather Tuesday afternoon\nthrough Wednesday morning, but then followed by another weather\nsystem from the northwest by Wednesday afternoon and lasting\nthrough Thursday. This next weather system will bring in more \nchances for periods of precipitation and snow across central and \nnorthern Nevada and keep temperatures just a few degrees below \nnormal. Winds also expected to elevate with this storm with\nhighest amounts across central Nevada coming from the south. \n\nFriday and into the next weekend, dry weather conditions return\nover Nevada with temperatures gradually warming up to near normal.\nLatest models are showing another low pressure system to the\nnorthwest along the Pacific coastline, but is not expected to push\ninto Nevada.",
